# One of the four roles from SP-A02-1. Which one a node takes is the boot value `role`, read from
# a credential by workpod-role-generator; the image is the same artifact either way (AB-A02-1).
#
# `all` is a single node carrying every slice at once — the shape a small installation runs in:
# the four layers of V-01 as the four slices of AP-3.1, and the whole A-04 sequence on one
# machine. An envelope arriving at intake and leaving as a patch, with no second node involved.
#
# What hangs here is Wants=, not Requires=: the role names what belongs to it, and the sequence's
# own Requires-chain (disk → selftest → register) is what enforces A-04. A failed step leaves the
# role standing and the failure named, instead of tearing the role down over it.

[Unit]
Description=Workpod node role: all
Documentation=https://github.com/Cheety/warft/blob/main/01-specification.md
Wants=workpod-control.slice workpod-captain.slice workpod-knowledge.slice workpod-work.slice
Wants=workpod-disk.service workpod-db.service workpod-selftest.service
Wants=workpod-control.service workpod-worker.service
